I'm sorry for the confusion but adding a dark mode toggle button requirement doesn't have anything to do with the `package.json` file.

The requirement you are asking for is a feature that pertains to user interface thus it should be implemented in the React components or in the CSS files. 

However, if you need any package that helps to implement dark mode, like `dark-mode-switch`, you can add this into your `package.json` dependencies.

Just like this,

{
  "name": "ps",
  "version": "0.1.0",
  "private": true,
  "dependencies": {
    "@emotion/styled": "^10.0.27",
    "@testing-library/jest-dom": "^4.2.4",
    "@testing-library/react": "^9.3.2",
    "@testing-library/user-event": "^7.1.2",
    "d3": "^6.2.0",
    "framer-motion": "^2.9.1",
    "normalize.css": "^8.0.1",
    "react": "^16.13.1",
    "react-dom": "^16.13.1",
    "react-scripts": "3.4.3",
    "rss-parser": "^3.9.0",
    "rss-to-json": "^1.0.5",
    "styled-components": "^5.2.0",
    "dark-mode-switch": "^1.0.1"
  },
  "scripts": {
    "start": "react-scripts start",
    "build": "react-scripts build",
    "test": "react-scripts test",
    "eject": "react-scripts eject"
  },
  "eslintConfig": {
    "extends": "react-app"
  },
  "browserslist": {
    "production": [
      ">0.2%",
      "not dead",
      "not op_mini all"
    ],
    "development": [
      "last 1 chrome version",
      "last 1 firefox version",
      "last 1 safari version"
    ]
  }
}

Adding `dark-mode-switch` package will allow you to use dark mode toggle functionality. After adding the package, don't forget to run `npm install` or `yarn install` command to install the added package. But keep in mind, you still need to work on UI components to fully implement the dark mode toggle button. 

